From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report charge for SM8350-style firmware

The battery unit is only set from the SC8280XP-style info response, so
on SM8350/SM8550 it stays at mWh and charge_full / charge_full_design
return -ENODATA. With no charge or energy values UPower reports 0 Wh and
cannot estimate time remaining (KDE's battery applet shows none).

SM8350-style firmware reports charge in uAh: set the unit accordingly,
and expose charge_now on SM8550 backed by the charge counter (the
remaining charge in uAh).
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -439,6 +439,7 @@
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP] = BATT_TEMP,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TECHNOLOGY] = BATT_TECHNOLOGY,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_COUNTER] =  BATT_CHG_COUNTER,
+	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW] =  BATT_CHG_COUNTER,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CYCLE_COUNT] = BATT_CYCLE_COUNT,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN] =  BATT_CHG_FULL_DESIGN,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL] = BATT_CHG_FULL,
@@ -583,7 +584,12 @@
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW:
 		if (unit != QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh)
 			return -ENODATA;
-		val->intval = battmgr->status.capacity;
+		/* SM8350-style firmware: remaining charge is the charge counter */
+		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350 ||
+		    battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550)
+			val->intval = battmgr->info.charge_count;
+		else
+			val->intval = battmgr->status.capacity;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_COUNTER:
 		val->intval = battmgr->info.charge_count;
@@ -911,6 +917,7 @@
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CYCLE_COUNT,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MODEL_NAME,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TIME_TO_FULL_AVG,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TIME_TO_EMPTY_AVG,
@@ -1658,6 +1665,15 @@
 	else
 		battmgr->variant = QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350;
 
+	/*
+	 * Only the SC8280XP-style info message carries a power unit. SM8350-style
+	 * firmware reports charge properties in uAh; without this the unit stays
+	 * mWh and charge_full/charge_full_design read as -ENODATA.
+	 */
+	if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350 ||
+	    battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550)
+		battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
+
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_charge_control_thresholds_init(battmgr);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
